# XSH pthread_testcancel()
# (pthread_setcancelstate() and pthread_setcanceltype(), on the same page,
# are the xsh/pthread_setcancelstate module)
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.pthread_testcancel.001
anchor     functions/pthread_testcancel.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/V2_chap02.html#2.9.5.2
class      required
since      2008
says       A thread with the default cancelability (enabled, deferred)
           that calls pthread_testcancel() after a request was made
           against it does not return from the call: its cleanup handler
           runs and pthread_join() gives PTHREAD_CANCELED.
test       t/001-acts.c

assertion  XSH.pthread_testcancel.002
anchor     functions/pthread_testcancel.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       With no request made against it, a thread's
           pthread_testcancel() returns, and the thread ends with the
           value it returns.
test       t/002-nothing-pending.c

assertion  XSH.pthread_testcancel.003
anchor     functions/pthread_testcancel.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/V2_chap02.html#2.9.5.1
class      required
since      2008
says       A thread with cancelability disabled and a request pending
           returns from two pthread_testcancel() calls; after it enables
           cancelability, its next pthread_testcancel() acts on the
           request (PTHREAD_CANCELED).
test       t/003-disabled.c
